<description>
Draw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.

Input structure:
- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.
- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.

Rule:
- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.
- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.
- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.

Key insight:
The marker's column is the route spine; its central vs off-center placement selects which opposite corner pair gets the horizontal edge segments.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single non-background marker pixel in an otherwise solid background grid",
  "path": "vertical route through the marker's column, plus horizontal edge segments to an opposite corner pair",
  "trajectory": "paint route background pixels blue",
  "dst": "connect to top-right and bottom-left corners if the marker is in the unique center column; otherwise connect to top-left and bottom-right corners",
  "transform": "preserve the marker color and leave all non-route background pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, N x N where N = 5-8 [observed]; N >= 2 (solver assert)
  background: solid single color, any color except blue (1)
  marker:
    count: exactly 1 non-background pixel
    color: any color except blue (1) and except the background color
    position: interior only (not on any border row/col) [observed]; any cell works for solver
  output_rule: |
    Paint the marker's column blue (top to bottom).
    If W is odd AND marker is in the center column (c == W//2):
      paint top row from c..W-1 blue (toward top-right corner)
      paint bottom row from 0..c blue (toward bottom-left corner)
    Else:
      paint top row from 0..c blue (toward top-left corner)
      paint bottom row from c..W-1 blue (toward bottom-right corner)
    Restore the marker pixel to its original color.
  output_shape: same as input
  blue_pixel_count: H + (top_segment_len - 1) + (bot_segment_len - 1) - 1

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is trivial -- solid grid + 1 marker)
  steps:
    - pick N in 5-10, create N x N grid of a random bg color (not blue/1)
    - choose the center-column branch and off-center branch with approximately equal probability
    - for the center-column branch, pick an odd N and set c = N//2; for the off-center branch, pick any N and choose an interior c that is not the center column when N is odd
    - pick a random interior row r where 0 < r < N-1
    - pick a marker color != bg and != blue (1)
    - place marker at (r, c)
  notes: |
    No output-first needed: input is just a solid grid with one pixel changed.
    The center-column branch triggers when N is odd and c == N//2;
